maml:description.maml:para:
Prepares the local computer to be managed remotely by PSWindowsUpdateNext. The cmdlet:

- creates or enables the Windows Firewall rule group PSWindowsUpdateNext, with an inbound rule that allows RPC dynamic ports for dllhost.exe (needed for DCOM calls to the Windows Update Agent);
- enables the Remote Scheduled Tasks Management and Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) firewall rule groups;
- sets the Remote Registry service start mode to Automatic if it is Disabled, and starts it if it is stopped;
- turns on Windows PowerShell remoting by running Enable-PSRemoting -Force in Windows PowerShell (with -SkipNetworkProfileCheck when you use -WinRMPublic) and starts the WinRM service;
- only with -LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy, sets the LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy registry value to 1 and the ForceGuest value to 0.

On computers that are not in a domain, Enable-PSRemoting itself sets LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy to 1. Without -LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy, the cmdlet restores the value that was there before. The cmdlet does not change the WinRM client TrustedHosts list.

These changes lower the security of the computer. Use the cmdlet only in a managed environment, and review the notes before you run it.

maml:introduction.maml:para:
```powershell
Install-WindowsUpdate -ComputerName PC02 -MicrosoftUpdate -AcceptAll -AutoReboot -SendReport -PSWUSettings @{ SmtpServer = 'smtp.contoso.com'; From = 'wu@contoso.com'; To = 'admins@contoso.com'; Port = 25 }
```

```powershell
if (Get-WURebootStatus -Silent) { 'Restart pending' }
```
